ow their problems  present potential solutions and see if  they're interested in it or not the best  feedback you'll get is going to come  from potential customers I made this  mistake early on in my software company  I spent tons of time working on this  feature that I thought my customers  wanted it's the most complicated feature  in our software and it turns out they  didn't really care and luckily I had  enough other great stuff in my software  they'll make it work  but a lot of entres make that mistake  you know learn from my mistake build  your business around your customer and  find out you know you want to know if  it's a good idea find out someone's  willing to pay you for it and the best  way to get started if you're going to  bootstrap is around the service you may  have a great product idea you may not  want to trade your time for money but at  the start you got to get close to your  customers and you got to keep your costs  down and that comes from starting the  service find a potential customer with a  problem and offer to help solve it for  them see what they think am I starting a  service it does a couple things it gets  you close to your customers it gets you  to really understand that their problems  if it's their business or their personal  life what their challenges are and how  you can help it also brings in  consistent revenue for you you're  keeping your cost down you're bringing  wrapping you in you're getting to the  point of survival where you have to go  back and get a job again working for  some way that you hate doing something  that's beneath you and and watching  other people make big dollars off of  your idea you need to get money coming  in and that starts from having a service  if you have consistent cash flow coming  in then that gives you the platform for  growth if that's launching product if  that's launching new services as I bring  it on a team that that's growing beyond  your local market whatever it is growth  so you're asking all the right questions  this is great i'm excited for you i hope  you'll take those steps start by talking  to your customers see what they think  see which there was they like best and  start again with that service instead of  the product to help you bootstrap it up  for everybody who's watching if you're  in the same situation you do not need a  lot of money to start a business the  guys who spend a lot of money often lose  a lot of money it doesn't guarantee your  success by any means successful  entrepreneurs by the most part if you  research their stories look at any  famous entrepreneur look up to for the  most part they started with nothing it  was them in a dream and a lot of hard  work and you can do the same good luck  for those of you watching if you liked  the video you know the drill thumbs up  below thank you so much you love seeing  them come in and I'd love to know what  you think about the video please leave a  comment below or you have a question  about your own company please leave in  the comment section below i really love  seemed to come in and i check those  every day so thank you and I'll see you  on next
 

